# 🚀 End-to-End Observability Stack (Production-Style Documentation)

## 📌 Overview

This document describes how to set up a complete observability stack in Kubernetes:

* **Metrics** → Prometheus
* **Logs** → Loki + Promtail
* **Tracing** → OpenTelemetry + Jaeger
* **Visualization** → Grafana

---

# 🧱 ARCHITECTURE

```
Applications
   │
   ├── Metrics → Prometheus → Grafana
   ├── Logs → Promtail → Loki → Grafana
   └── Traces → OTEL Collector → Jaeger → Grafana (optional)
```

---

# ⚙️ 1. PREREQUISITES

* Kubernetes cluster (1 master + workers)
* Helm installed
* StorageClass available (`local-path`)

Check:

```bash
kubectl get storageclass
```

---

# 📊 2. INSTALL PROMETHEUS + GRAFANA

```bash
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update
```

```bash
helm install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack -n monitoring --create-namespace
```

---

## 🔓 Expose Grafana

```bash
kubectl edit svc monitoring-grafana -n monitoring
```

Set:

```yaml
type: NodePort
nodePort: 30000
```

Access:

```
http://<NODE-IP>:30000
```

---

# 📦 3. INSTALL LOKI (WITH PVC)

## ✅ loki-values.yaml

```yaml
deploymentMode: SingleBinary

singleBinary:
  replicas: 1

backend:
  replicas: 0

read:
  replicas: 0

write:
  replicas: 0

gateway:
  enabled: false

chunksCache:
  enabled: false

resultsCache:
  enabled: false

loki:
  auth_enabled: false
  commonConfig:
    replication_factor: 1
  storage:
    type: filesystem

  schemaConfig:
    configs:
      - from: "2024-01-01"
        store: tsdb
        object_store: filesystem
        schema: v13
        index:
          prefix: index_
          period: 24h

persistence:
  enabled: true
  size: 10Gi
  storageClassName: local-path
```

---

## Install Loki

```bash
helm repo add grafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

helm install loki grafana/loki -n monitoring -f loki-values.yaml
```

---

## ✅ Verify

```bash
kubectl get pods -n monitoring | grep loki
```

Expected:

```
loki-0   1/1 Running
```

